cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Please cite the original thesis when discussing this research. Cite Voteview
  separately for its source data, and include the Congress and retrieval date
  when reporting results from the refreshed research companion.
type: software
title: "Eigenpolitics: Research Companion to Eigen-Politics"
repository-code: "https://github.com/maxchelminski/eigenpolitics"
url: "https://maxchelminski.github.io/eigenpolitics/"
authors:
  - family-names: Chelminski
    given-names: Maximilian
abstract: >-
  An interactive atlas of U.S. Senate voting networks across 119 Congresses,
  with original and shared-senator-aligned spectral maps, graph connectivity,
  brokerage, and a reproducible Voteview refresh pipeline. Developed from
  Maximilian Chelminski's 2026 master's thesis, the repository preserves the
  original research alongside a maintained companion. Refreshed results are
  not an exact reproduction of the original thesis snapshot.
keywords:
  - spectral graph theory
  - United States Senate
  - political polarization
  - roll-call voting
  - graph Laplacian
preferred-citation:
  type: thesis
  title: "Eigen-Politics: A Spectral Analysis of the US Senate"
  authors:
    - family-names: Chelminski
      given-names: Maximilian
  year: 2026
  thesis-type: "Master's thesis"
  institution:
    name: "Graduate School of Arts and Sciences, Quantitative Methods in the Social Sciences"
